Description: avcodec/vvc: retain EOS for the following access unit
 The NAL loop writes last_eos after decoding the picture in the packet.
 The next packet overwrites it from eos, which remains zero, so a CRA
 following EOS is not recognized as the start of a new coded layer video
 sequence. Reusing a POC then drops the picture with a duplicate-POC
 error.
 .
 Set the current packet's eos flag instead, so the following access unit
 gets NoOutputBeforeRecoveryFlag as required by H.266 8.1.1. Only retain
 EOS for the supported layer 0; another layer's EOS does not end layer
 0's CLVS (H.266 7.4.3.11).
 .
 Two CRA-only excerpts of RAP_A_1 separated by EOS now output both
 pictures, matching two independent decodes. Master outputs only the
 first picture and can still exit successfully.
 .
